# Molten Duplication on Mine Raider: the token is a copy, so it enters and Mine Raider's "When this creature enters, if you control another outlaw"
# trigger fires for it (CR 603.6a); the original Mine Raider (Human Rogue) is the other outlaw (CR 700.12a), so one Treasure is made. The Raider
# cast alone made no Treasure (nothing else was an outlaw), which checks the "another" half of the condition.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mountain
Mine Raider
Molten Duplication
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mine Raider.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Molten Duplication.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mine Raider)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mine Raider#2.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mine Raider#2.Types = Creature; Artifact
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mine Raider#2.Keywords = Haste; Trample
[T1 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Subtypes = Treasure
Bot1.Battlefield.Mine Raider#2 = (absent)
